cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Actor-Critic vs. Dynamic Programming for Bridge-Element Maintenance Planning"
abstract: >-
  Reinforcement learning (PPO actor-critic) and dynamic programming baselines
  for life-cycle-cost-optimal maintenance of deteriorating bridge elements
  modeled as a Markov decision process, with interpretable soft/oblique
  decision-tree policies and MLE/method-of-moments fitting of the initial
  condition-state distribution from National Bridge Element inspection data.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Moayyedi
    given-names: Amir
    email: s.amir.h.moayyedi@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SAMIRHOSEIN/actCrit-vs-DynPrg-RL-MLE"
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - dynamic programming
  - proximal policy optimization
  - bridge maintenance
  - infrastructure asset management
  - life-cycle cost
  - Markov decision process
  - interpretable machine learning
